// uwkit provider — FLAT. The surface is a plane at sea level.
//
// The baseline every other provider is judged against, and deliberately the dullest thing
// that can satisfy the contract. Its job in proof 3 is to make the failure mode visible: a
// flat sea would let a hardcoded constant pass every test, so if swapping to a real
// provider does NOT change the boundary, the swap is not doing anything.
float uw_surface_height(vec2 world_xz) {
	return p.wave.x;
}
